            "role": "user",
            "content": "find me the law on public defamation"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "Malaysian law addresses defamation through both civil and criminal provisions. The Defamation Act 1957 governs civil liability and privileges for certain publications, while the Penal Code creates criminal offences for defamation and related publication offences. The Printing Presses and Publications Act 1984 adds a specific offence for maliciously publishing false news.\n\n---\n*This information is for legal research only and does not constitute legal advice. Please consult a qualified Malaysian lawyer for advice on your specific situation.*",
